<title>USA: Sheldahl weighs China expansion.</title>
<headline>Sheldahl weighs China expansion.</headline>
<dateline>NORTHFIELD, Minn. 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sheldahl Inc said Tuesday it is studying the feasibility of expanding its manufacturing operations in China.</p>
<p>Sheldahl said it hired ITN Inc, a Thousand Oaks, Calif.-based consulting company, to assist it. ITN specializes in assisting U.S. companies in China ventures.</p>
<p>Sheldahl currently is a joint venture partner in a laminate manufacturing facility in China. The plant will begin pilot production this spring.</p>
<p>Sheldahl makes flexible printed circuitry, flexible laminates and high-density substrates for the automotive electronics and data communications markets.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
